Package: learnr2
Title: Interactive Tutorials with Quarto and WebR
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("David", "Kane", , "dave.kane@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Create interactive R tutorials that run entirely in the
    browser using Quarto and WebR via the 'quarto-live' extension. Provides
    learnr-style authoring conveniences -- scaffolding, exercises, hints,
    solutions, and quizzes -- without Shiny, R Markdown, or a server.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
RoxygenNote: 7.3.3
Imports:
    fs,
    htmltools,
    jsonlite,
    knitr,
    quarto
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Quarto command line tool
    (https://github.com/quarto-dev/quarto-cli).
URL: https://github.com/davidkane9/learnr2
BugReports: https://github.com/davidkane9/learnr2/issues
